ogi, Uganda: plants, use and administration</article-title><source>Journal of Ethnopharmacology</source><year>2003</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12902048</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-8741(03)00161-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamatenesi-Mugisha</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Oryem-Origa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medicinal plants used to induce labour during childbirth in western Uganda</article-title><source>Journal of Ethnopharmacology</source><year>2007</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16901666</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jep.2006.06.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jari&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Popovi&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma&#x000e8;ukanovi&#x000e6;-Joci&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Djurdjevi&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mijatovi&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Karad&#x0017e;i&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitrovi&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pavlovi&#x000e6;</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An ethnobotanical study on the usage of wild medicinal herbs from Kopaonik Mountain (Central Serbia)</article-title><source>Journal of Ethnopharmacology</source><year>2007</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17145148</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jep.2006.11.007</pub-id></citation>